defmodule NativeSets do
  # Sets and streams (spec/alchem-sets-streams.md).
  #
  # set[T] is tag 25 and its element: at run time a map from the elements to
  # true, so the map routines keep it in order and library/MapSet.alc is
  # written over maps. stream[T] is tag 26 and its element: a function value
  # of no parameters that gives none at the end, or some({element, rest}) with
  # the stream of what follows. A range is first, last and step behind a
  # count of 0, or behind the list of its integers once it was needed.
  #
  # Each of the routines below takes a value in RAX and leaves one there.
  # first, last and step from the stack: the range, with step 0 as 1 or -1.
  # A fifth word keeps R9 when the step was 0, else 0: where a step was
  # written (nk_range), which a range written as a stream names when its
  # step is 0 (zf_stepped).
  def nn_range_emit(): bytes do
    b[65,88,94,95,77,133,192,116,5,69,49,201,235,19,73,199,192,1,0,0,0,72,57,247,126,7,73,199,192,255,255,255,255,77,141,92,36,40,77,57,235,118,7,255,20,37,120,4,64,0,76,137,224,15,31,68,0,0,77,137,220,72,199,0,0,0,0,0,72,137,120,8,72,137,112,16,76,137,64,24,76,137,72,32]
  end
  # A range with the list of its integers before first, last and step.
  def nn_range_list(): bytes do
